{'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 7, 10, 10, 37, 32, 309947, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'task_id': '7c81336cd8d0', 'workflow_id': '14e49b5790f1472f', 'iteration': 2, 'files': [{'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 7, 10, 10, 37, 32, 309928, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'path': 'palindrome.py', 'content': 'def is_palindrome(s: str) -> bool:\n    """\n    Check if a string is a palindrome, ignoring case, spaces, and punctuation.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string to check.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the string is a palindrome after normalization, False otherwise.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> is_palindrome("A man, a plan, a canal: Panama")\n        True\n        >>> is_palindrome("race a car")\n        False\n        >>> is_palindrome(" ")\n        True\n    """\n    # Filter alphanumeric characters and convert to lowercase\n    cleaned = \'\'.join(char.lower() for char in s if char.isalnum())\n    # Check if cleaned string reads the same forwards and backwards\n    return cleaned == cleaned[::-1]\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    # Test cases\n    assert is_palindrome("A man, a plan, a canal: Panama") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("race a car") is False\n    assert is_palindrome(" ") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("Madam") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("No lemon, no melon") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("Hello, World!") is False\n    assert is_palindrome("") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("a") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("ab") is False\n\n    print("All tests passed!")'}], 'explanation': 'Fixed the syntax error in the print statement by ensuring the closing quote is on the same line. The function correctly normalizes the input string by keeping only alphanumeric characters and converting to lowercase, then checks if it equals its reverse. Includes 9 assert-based tests covering various edge cases.'}